Notice something beautiful.

Every RFC we've written now naturally belongs to one or more Memory Spaces.

That means the RFCs are converging into a coherent architecture rather than remaining isolated concepts.

Another improvement

I think we should formally introduce Memory Activation.

One weakness of almost every AI memory framework today is that retrieval is binary:

Search

↓

Results

Humans don't retrieve memories that way.

Instead:

Stimulus

↓

Activation spreads

↓

Related concepts activate

↓

Attention focuses

↓

Reasoning begins

MOS should model this.

For example:

Question:

"How should I deploy PostgreSQL?"

This shouldn't only retrieve "PostgreSQL."

It should activate:

Docker
Kubernetes
Previous deployments
Backup procedures
Security policies
Cost constraints
Resource history
Similar failures
Learned optimizations

This is activation, not retrieval.

This single concept could become one of the distinguishing features of MOS.

